# 09b round-12 distinguishing ablations of clean payload C10 (rerun: payload unchanged, evidence regenerated)

Payload C10: d1fcffdf8b3f411ecde28ae0b14fe79523dfcc14 (unchanged; fresh rerun for validation-12).
Each ablation changes exactly one behaviour in a detached worktree at C10, runs
packages/kernel/tests/*.test.ts against it, and is reverted before the next.
The exact edit script, its diff, the full run output and the parsed rejection are recorded
per ablation below. An ablation is REJECTED when named packet cases fail; that is what makes
those cases distinguishing rather than merely green.

XA/XB guard K11-R7-STATE-03 (install/restore direction). X1/X7/X3/X4/X8 re-prove the
own-data family guards. Guards for code no correction round touches (holey scratch X2, dual
serializer layers X5, frozen vocabulary X6, Map/freeze S1/S2, primordial prototype V3,
exact-JCS-call N1, single bound observation N3, descriptor agreement P1, JCS pin JCS,
over-limit traversal) are unchanged between C9 and C10 apart from the descriptor they convert
through; their round-9 runs (validation-09/09b) remain committed as their own round's
evidence and are not claimed as this candidate's reruns.

